course: dictionary
lesson: 8213
title: Retro words and old styles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a style that came from another time. Retro means copying or looking like the style of the past, especially the 1950s to 1990s. «Leo's console was his uncle's old one, and the kids laughed at the blocky graphics» gives you the clue: the console is old, and the graphics look old too.
explain: Look at the words after the clue. «Until they found the old two-player games were hilarious» tells you the kids enjoyed those old games. Then «the retro ones» means the old-style games. Check it: swap «old-style» in for retro, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Retro can also mean old-fashioned in a fun or cool way. The old style is chosen on purpose, so a retro game is a new-style copy of an old game, or an old game that people enjoy again. When you see retro, ask yourself: is this old style being copied or enjoyed on purpose?
fact: Retro means copying or looking like the style of the past, especially the 1950s to 1990s.
fact: Retro can describe clothes, games, music and furniture that look old on purpose.
fact: Informally, retro means old-fashioned in a fun or cool way.
fact: The prefix «retro-» means backwards, as in «retrograde» and «retrospective».
fact: Retro can also be a noun, as in «go retro», but it has no plural, so you do not say two retros.
exercise: What does retro mean? | Very fast in a race | Brand new and never used before | *Copying the style of the past | Found under the sea
exercise: «The old two-player games were hilarious.» What does hilarious mean? | Very old | Very quiet | *Very funny | Very sad
exercise: The prefix retro- means what? | Under the water | *Backwards | Very big | Forwards
test: Which best describes a retro diner? | *Copies the style of the past | Sells only salad | Was built last week | Is under water
test: Which is a retro game? | *An old-style game copied from the 1980s | A new game with 3D virtual reality | A game with no rules | A game you play in the sea
exam: «Come round for the retro ones» means come round for which games? | *Old-style | Brand-new | Broken | Sleepy
